/* The AT link on the nRF54LM20 DK. Same shape as the nRF54L15 DK overlay
 * next to this file: uart20 is the board's console/shell/mcumgr UART
 * (nrf54lm20_a_b_cpuapp_common.dtsi chooses it), so the AT link takes
 * uart30, the second VCOM, which the DK's own pinctrl already routes
 * (P0.06 TX, P0.07 RX, P0.08 RTS, P0.09 CTS in
 * nrf54lm20dk_nrf54lm20_a_b-pinctrl.dtsi). The board dtsi already gives
 * uart30 its pinctrl states and a 115200 default; only the chosen node
 * and the status are ours.
 *
 * WHAT THIS OVERLAY DELIBERATELY DOES NOT CARRY, since the nRF54L15
 * arms carry all three and copying them here would be wrong:
 *
 * - No `&cpuapp_sram` reclaim. On the nRF54L15 the SoC dtsi hands cpuapp
 *   only 188 KB of the 256 KB die and reserves the rest for the cpuflpr
 *   VPR, so both L15 boards reclaim it by hand. On this part
 *   nrf54lm20_a_b.dtsi already spans the whole 511 KB with cpuapp_sram
 *   and nrf54lm20_a_b_cpuapp.dtsi deletes cpuflpr_sram outright, so
 *   cpuapp owns 523,264 B with no overlay at all. Nordic's own Matter
 *   template overlay for this board has no &cpuapp_sram block either.
 *
 * - No `&hfxo` load-capacitor block. The Ophelia-IV needed one because
 *   its module carries no capacitor programming of its own, and the
 *   omission cost a bench session (radio silent, everything else
 *   healthy). This DK programs the identical 15,000 fF internal caps in
 *   nrf54lm20_a_b_cpuapp_common.dtsi, and 17,000 fF on the LFXO.
 *
 * - No LFCLK source guard. The Ophelia-IV has no 32 kHz crystal, so its
 *   board CMakeLists.txt fails the build if the RC source is not
 *   selected. This DK has an LFXO crystal and configures it; carrying
 *   the guard here would enforce the wrong choice on hardware that has
 *   the right one.
 *
 * The RRAM is also left at its 1940 KB default rather than reclaimed to
 * 2036 KB: the 96 KB tail belongs to the cpuflpr, nothing here runs on
 * it, and the partition map beside this file already leaves 52.9 percent
 * of the 1854 KB app slot unused (894,904 B used, measured 2026-08-31).
 * Reclaiming it is a decision for the round that needs the space.
 */
/ {
    chosen {
        hearth,at-uart = &uart30;
    };
};

&uart30 {
    status = "okay";
    current-speed = <115200>;
};
